  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "The dry cargo market underwent a five-day decline before recovering towards the end of the \nweek. The Baltic Dry Index (BDI) closed today at 3,370 points, reflecting a decrease of 3.91% compared \nto last Friday's closing value of 3,507 points. \n \nBaltic Dry Index           3370  +34 \nBaltic Capesize Index  5768 +112 \nBaltic Panamax Index    2251  -31 \nBaltic Supramax Index  1767   +5 \nBaltic Handysize Index    988   +8 \n \nThe bulker S+P market remains strong, though it was somewhat quieter this week, with a total of 15 \ntransactions recorded, comprising 2 kamsarmaxes, 2 panamax, 1 ultramax, 5 Supramaxes, 1 Handymax \nand 4 Handysize bulk carriers.",
    "tankers": "Emirati buyers (clients of Onex) are reported to have scooped up this week four VLCCs - \nASHOKA, NISSOS HERACLEA, XI XIU and DENNIE - as well as two Suezmaxes, EVRIDIKI \nand ORFEAS at firm levels. \n \nFor a detailed review and additional information regarding these week's transactions, kindly refer to our \n\"representative sales\" section.",
    "demolition": "The Subcontinent markets remain stable overall without many reported deals. For an \noverview of demolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
